#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Bookkeeping in plan/, without hand edits. The plan of a requirement is plan/plan.json (the
graph and the state of the run) and plan/<ID>.json (the items of each node); the schema is
scripts/lib/plan.schema.json, the rules are in scripts/lib/plandata.py.

Each write changes plan/ in one place, checks the change with scripts/check-plan, and writes it.
Add --commit to commit it (one commit, a standard message). Add --dry-run to print the diff and
change nothing. Coordinator commands run only on main; slice owner commands only on the branch
of that slice. Each refusal says the next step.

Read-only (anywhere):
  plan show <ID>                       the node: state, scope, items, log
  plan title [--milestone M1]          the coordinator status title, counted from the states
  plan lint                            check plan/ (exit 1)
  plan dag [--json]                    the graph of plan/plan.json (nodes, edges, order); a cycle,
        an unknown need or a schema error makes it fail
  plan passed <ID> [--json] [--base REF]   passed of each item of <ID>, derived from the
        verifier results for the head commit of its branch (scripts/lib/plandata.py); results
        for an older commit are stale and count for nothing. The branch and the items come from
        plan/ as committed at REF (default HEAD), never from an uncommitted edit

Verifier (not the slice owner):
  plan verify <ID> [--base REF]        check out the head commit of the branch of <ID> (from
        plan/plan.json as committed at REF, default HEAD) clean, run the `cmd:` evidence of each
        item there (and check `commit:` pointers), and store the commands and exit codes as a
        git note on that commit. The only way to make results: no command takes them from
        outside. A `cmd:` is a repo-relative executable file of the commit, with no symlink in
        its path. Logs: /tmp/dshm-verify/

Merge step (the coordinator, or the merge node of the Workflow):
  plan merge <ID> --into <branch> [--allow-changed-evidence PATH] [--dry-run]
        merge the branch of <ID> into <branch> only if the checks pass on the merge commit.
        It always runs the copy of these tools committed at the tip of <branch> (it starts that
        copy from a clean checkout when the running copy differs), takes the branch and the
        items from plan/ as committed there (the slice branch may only add evidence), makes the
        merge commit in a clean checkout, runs the evidence on it, stores the results on the
        merge commit, and then moves <branch> to it. It reads no report and no earlier results.
        A protected evidence file that the branch changes or deletes stops the merge: a reviewer
        or the user must look at it. Protected: each file of the target that a `cmd:` names (the
        executable, a file argument, or a path that such a script names), every file of the
        target in the directory of a `cmd:` file and below it (a file at the top of the repo
        protects only itself), and scripts/lib/. It does not follow calls. After that, the coordinator passes
        --allow-changed-evidence <path> (repeatable); the merge commit message records it. New
        evidence files of the branch are listed as "new evidence, judged by the reviewer".
        Prints a JSON summary; exit 0 = merged (--dry-run: passed), 1 = not

Coordinator (on main):
  plan new "<title>"                   start the plan of a requirement that the user has set
        (refused if plan/plan.json exists). Title: "M3 · Push and replies"
  plan add tracer|spike|slice "<name>" --why T --cuts T --done "[auto] …" [--done …]
        [--needs "T0, X1"] [--demo PATH] [--not T]
        add a node: the next ID (T0, X1, S1, …), state todo, its items in plan/<ID>.json.
        A slice needs the first tracer unless --needs says otherwise. --cuts - reads stdin
  plan add exit "<item>"               add a [human] exit item
  plan row <ID> <status> [--next T]    change the state of a node (updated = today)
  plan log "<title>" [--body T|-]      add a plan log entry (- = body from stdin)
  plan pending <slice> <kind> "<item>" [--branch B] [--commit-ref C]   add what waits for the user
  plan fix "<name>" --bug "<what the user saw>" [--needs ID]
        a bug that the user reported: add a fix slice (the next S number); then `plan assign`
        and start a session for it. The coordinator does not fix code.
  plan assign <ID> --branch B [--worktree P] [--from C] [--note T]
        give the slice its branch (in plan/plan.json) and its resources (scripts/slice-env),
        set it to doing, add the log entry
  plan merged <ID> <merge-commit> [--note T] [--keep]
        after a merge: check plan/ of the merge commit against its first parent; set the node
        to review (open [human] items) or done, with the merge commit; add pending entries for
        its open [human] items and for each provisional choice that the merge added to
        ARCHITECTURE.md; add the log entry with the review result from /tmp/dshm-review. Then
        the cleanup below; --keep skips it
  plan cleanup <ID>
        remove what a merged slice left on the Mac, and print each thing: the simulator dshm-<ID>;
        /tmp/dshm-<id> and /tmp/dshm-<id>-*; each worktree and branch of the slice whose HEAD is
        an ancestor of the merge commit (`cleanup`: of main) and that has no uncommitted or
        untracked file (`git worktree remove`, `git branch -d`, never forced); its DSHM_HOME if it
        is inside ~/.dshm/. A simulator that a running demo owns (/tmp/dshm-guard) and a /tmp path
        that a running process names stay. It prints what it leaves, and why. Only for a slice
        that is review or done. With DSHM_CLEANUP_DRY=1 or --dry-run it prints what it would
        remove and removes nothing

Slice owner (on the slice branch):
  plan evidence <ID> <item number> "<pointer>"   add an evidence pointer (cmd:, test:, commit:,
        shot:) to an [auto] or [ui] item. Only the verifier decides `passed`
  plan slice-log <ID> "<title>" [--body T|-]     add a dated entry to the log of the node
  plan slice-status <ID> <status>                the state of the node

The user (not an agent):
  plan accept <ID>|exit <item number> "<device or note>"   record a [human] item as accepted.
        It asks on the terminal (/dev/tty) and records only when the user types the ID back,
        so a shell with no terminal (an agent's) cannot record it

Exit 0 = OK, 1 = refused or check failed, 2 = usage.
"""

import argparse
import difflib
import glob
import json
import os
import re
import shutil
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
from pathlib import Path

sys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent / "lib"))
import dshm  # noqa: E402
import plandata  # noqa: E402

PlanError = dshm.PlanError
TRAILER = "\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>"
ID_RE = re.compile(r"\b[TXS]\d+\b")
# kind: (ID prefix, first number, title prefix)
KINDS = {"tracer": ("T", 0, "Tracer bullet: "), "spike": ("X", 1, "Spike: "), "slice": ("S", 1, "")}
MAX_ITEMS = {"T": 3, "S": 5}     # one session can finish a tracer or a slice; spikes have no limit
MARKS = {"done": "✅", "review": "👀", "doing": "🔨", "blocked": "⏸"}


class Plan:
    """plan/ of the working tree: plan.json and the items files, changed in memory, then saved."""

    def __init__(self, root):
        self.root = root
        self.dir = root / plandata.PLAN_DIR
        self.before = plandata_files(self.dir)
        self.exists = plandata.PLAN_FILE in self.before
        self.doc = json.loads(self.before[plandata.PLAN_FILE]) if self.exists else None
        self.slices = {}           # ID -> items doc, for each items file that a command changes
        # Other files to commit with plan/.
        self.extra_files = []

    def load(self):
        if not self.exists:
            raise PlanError(plandata.NO_PLAN)
        try:
            plandata.read_plan(self.root)
        except plandata.DataError as e:
            raise PlanError(str(e))
        return self

    def node(self, sid):
        try:
            return plandata.find_node(self.doc, sid)
        except plandata.DataError as e:
            raise PlanError(str(e))

    def items(self, sid):
        if sid not in self.slices:
            self.slices[sid] = json.loads(self.before[f"plan/{sid}.json"])
        return self.slices[sid]

    def after(self):
        out = dict(self.before)
        out[plandata.PLAN_FILE] = plandata.dump(self.doc)
        for sid, doc in self.slices.items():
            out[f"plan/{sid}.json"] = plandata.dump(doc)
        return out

    def save(self, args, message, agent=True):
        after = self.after()
        changed = sorted(p for p in after if after[p] != self.before.get(p))
        if not changed:
            print("plan: no change")
            return 0
        if args.dry_run:
            for p in changed:
                sys.stdout.writelines(difflib.unified_diff(
                    self.before.get(p, "").splitlines(True), after[p].splitlines(True), p, f"{p} (new)"))
            return 0
        check(self.root, self.before, after, agent)
        self.dir.mkdir(exist_ok=True)
        for p in changed:
            (self.root / p).write_text(after[p])
        print(f"plan: {', '.join(changed)} changed ({message})")
        if args.commit:
            files = [*changed, *self.extra_files]
            dshm.git("add", "--", *files, cwd=self.root)
            r = subprocess.run(["git", "commit", "-q", "-m", message + TRAILER, "--", *files],
                               cwd=self.root, capture_output=True, text=True)
            if r.returncode != 0:
                raise PlanError(f"git commit failed:\n{r.stdout}{r.stderr}\nNext: read the hook message above, "
                                f"repair what it names, and commit plan/ again")
            print(f"plan: committed {dshm.git('rev-parse', '--short', 'HEAD', cwd=self.root)} {message}")
        return 0


def plandata_files(d):
    if not d.is_dir():
        return {}
    return {f"{plandata.PLAN_DIR}/{p.name}": p.read_text() for p in sorted(d.iterdir()) if p.is_file()}


def check(root, before, after, agent=True):
    """scripts/check-plan on this one change (--agent: no human: pointer)."""
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as d:
        for name, files in (("base", before), ("new", after)):
            Path(d, name).mkdir()
            for p, text in files.items():
                Path(d, name, Path(p).name).write_text(text)
        argv = [str(root / "scripts/check-plan"), "--base", str(Path(d, "base")), "--new", str(Path(d, "new"))]
        r = subprocess.run(argv + (["--agent"] if agent else []), cwd=root, capture_output=True, text=True)
    if r.returncode != 0:
        raise PlanError("scripts/check-plan refused the change (nothing written):\n" + r.stdout + r.stderr)


def entry(title, body=""):
    title = " ".join(title.split()).rstrip(".")
    if not title:
        raise PlanError("the entry has no title. Next: give it a title")
    return {"date": dshm.today(), "title": title, "body": (body or "").strip("\n")}


def read_body(value):
    if value == "-":
        return sys.stdin.read()
    return value or ""


def need_main():
    b = dshm.branch()
    if b != "main":
        raise PlanError(f"this command is for the coordinator, on main (now on {b}). "
                        f"Next: run it in the main checkout, or ask the coordinator")


def need_slice_branch(sid):
    b = dshm.branch()
    key = sid.lower()
    if b == "main" or not re.search(rf"(^|/){re.escape(key)}(-|$)", b):
        raise PlanError(f"this command is for the owner of {sid}, on its branch (now on {b}). "
                        f"Next: run it in the worktree of {sid}, or ask the coordinator")


def set_state(node, status=None, nxt=None):
    if status:
        if status not in plandata.STATUSES:
            raise PlanError(f"status must be one of {', '.join(plandata.STATUSES)}. Next: use one of them")
        node["status"] = status
    if nxt is not None:
        node["next"] = nxt
    node["updated"] = dshm.today()


def parse_item(text):
    text = " ".join(text.split())
    m = re.match(r"^\[(auto|ui|human)\]\s+(.+)$", text)
    if not m:
        raise PlanError(f"an item starts with [auto], [ui] or [human]: {text!r}. Next: add the tier")
    return {"tier": m.group(1), "text": m.group(2).rstrip(), "files": [], "screens": [], "passed": False}


def item_at(items, n, sid):
    if not 1 <= n <= len(items):
        raise PlanError(f"{sid} has items 1 to {len(items)}, not {n}. Next: `scripts/plan show {sid}` lists them")
    return items[n - 1]


# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- commands

def cmd_show(p, a):
    n = p.node(a.id)
    print(f"{n['id']} · {n['title']}  [{n['kind']}]  {n.get('status', 'todo')}"
          f"  needs {', '.join(n['needs']) or '—'}  branch {n['branch'] or '—'}"
          + (f"  merged {n['merge']}" if n.get("merge") else ""))
    for k in ("why", "cuts", "not", "demo", "next"):
        if n.get(k):
            print(f"{k.capitalize()}: {n[k]}")
    print("Items:")
    for i, it in enumerate(p.items(a.id)["items"], 1):
        ev = " · ".join(it.get("evidence", []))
        print(f"  {i}. [{it['tier']}] {it['text']}" + (f" — {ev}" if ev else ""))
    for e in n.get("log", []):
        print(f"- {e['date']} · {e['title']}." + (f" {e['body']}" if e["body"] else ""))
    return 0


def title_from(doc, milestone):
    count = {k: 0 for k in MARKS}
    for n in doc["nodes"]:
        if n.get("status", "todo") in count:
            count[n.get("status", "todo")] += 1
    return f"🎛 Coordinator · {milestone} · " + " ".join(f"{MARKS[k]}{count[k]}" for k in MARKS)


def cmd_title(p, a):
    print(title_from(p.doc, a.milestone or p.doc["title"].split(" · ")[0]))
    return 0


def cmd_lint(p, a):
    errors = plandata.tree_errors(plandata.worktree_files(p.root))
    if not p.exists:
        errors = [plandata.NO_PLAN] + errors
    for e in errors:
        print(f"plan lint: {e}")
    if not errors:
        print("plan lint: OK")
    return 1 if errors else 0


def cmd_dag(p, a):
    try:
        g = plandata.dag(plandata.load_plan(p.root))
    except plandata.DataError as e:
        raise PlanError(str(e))
    if a.json:
        print(json.dumps(g, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False))
    else:
        for sid in g["order"]:
            n = next(n for n in g["nodes"] if n["id"] == sid)
            print(f"{sid}  {n.get('status', 'todo'):7} needs {', '.join(n['needs']) or '—'}  {n['title']}")
    return 0


def cmd_passed(p, a):
    try:
        d = plandata.derive(p.root, a.id, a.base)
    except plandata.DataError as e:
        raise PlanError(str(e))
    if a.json:
        print(json.dumps(d, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False))
        return 0
    head = d["head"][:12] if d["head"] else "no commit"
    who = f"verified by {d['verifier']} at {d['verified_at']}" if d["verifier"] else "no verifier results for this commit"
    print(f"{d['id']} · {d['branch'] or 'no branch'} @ {head} · {who}")
    if d["stale"]:
        print(f"  stale: results for {d['stale'][:12]} do not count for {head}")
    for it in d["items"]:
        mark = "x" if it["passed"] else " "
        runs = " · ".join(f"{r['cmd']} → {r['exit']}" for r in it["runs"])
        print(f"  [{mark}] [{it['tier']}] {it['text']}" + (f" — {runs}" if runs else ""))
    print(f"passed: {str(d['passed']).lower()}")
    return 0


def cmd_verify(p, a):
    try:
        res = plandata.verify(p.root, a.id, a.base, say=lambda m: print(f"plan: {m}", flush=True, file=sys.stderr))
    except plandata.DataError as e:
        raise PlanError(str(e))
    ok = sum(1 for r in res["items"] if plandata.item_passed(r))
    print(f"plan: verified {a.id} at {res['commit'][:12]}: {ok} of {len(res['items'])} items passed "
          f"({plandata.NOTES_REF})")
    return 0


def cmd_merge(p, a):
    root, say = p.root, (lambda m: print(f"plan: {m}", flush=True, file=sys.stderr))
    base = dshm.git("rev-parse", "-q", "--verify", f"refs/heads/{a.into}^{{commit}}", cwd=root, check=False)
    if not base:
        raise PlanError(f"no branch {a.into}. Next: give an existing target branch, for example --into main")
    here = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent
    if not plandata.same_as(root, base, here):
        # Not the copy of the tools at the tip of the target: run that copy instead.
        say(f"running the merge tools of {a.into} at {base[:12]}")
        with plandata.Checkout(root, base, f"merge-tools-{a.id.lower()}") as wt:
            argv = [sys.executable, str(wt / "scripts/plan"), "merge", a.id, "--into", a.into]
            argv += [x for f in a.allow for x in ("--allow-changed-evidence", f)]
            return subprocess.run(argv + (["--dry-run"] if a.dry_run else []), cwd=wt).returncode
    try:
        res = plandata.merge(root, a.id, a.into, dry=a.dry_run, allow=a.allow, say=say)
    except plandata.DataError as e:
        raise PlanError(str(e))
    print(json.dumps(res, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False))
    for f in res["new_evidence"]:
        say(f"new evidence, judged by the reviewer: {f}")
    for f in res["allowed_changed_evidence"]:
        say(f"changed evidence allowed by --allow-changed-evidence: {f}")
    ok = res["passed"] if a.dry_run else res["merged"]
    say(("passed" if a.dry_run else f"merged {a.id} into {a.into} as {res['merge'][:12]}") if ok
        else f"not merged: the checks failed on the merge commit {res['merge'][:12]}")
    return 0 if ok else 1



def cmd_new(p, a):
    """Start the plan of a requirement that the user has set."""
    need_main()
    if p.exists:
        raise PlanError("plan/plan.json exists: one requirement at a time. Next: when its exit "
                        "passes, the user removes plan/; then start the next one")
    title = " ".join(a.title.split())
    if not title:
        raise PlanError("the plan has no title. Next: give one, for example \"M3 · Push and replies\"")
    p.doc = {"title": title, "nodes": [], "exit": [], "log": [entry("Plan started", title)], "pending": []}
    return p.save(a, f"Plan: start {title}")


def next_id(doc, kind):
    prefix, first, _ = KINDS[kind]
    nums = [int(n["id"][1:]) for n in doc["nodes"] if n["id"].startswith(prefix)]
    return f"{prefix}{max(nums) + 1 if nums else first}"


def add_node(p, kind, name, needs=None, why="", cuts="", demo="", done=(), not_="",
             nxt="Assign it and start a session"):
    """Add a tracer, spike or slice: the next ID, state todo, the items file. Returns the ID."""
    doc = p.doc
    sid = next_id(doc, kind)
    prefix, _, title_prefix = KINDS[kind]
    name = " ".join(name.split()).rstrip(".")
    if not name:
        raise PlanError("the node has no name. Next: give it a name")
    if title_prefix and not name.startswith(title_prefix):
        name = title_prefix + name
    known = [n["id"] for n in doc["nodes"]]
    if needs is None:   # a slice needs the first tracer, unless it says otherwise
        tracers = sorted((x for x in known if x.startswith("T")), key=lambda x: int(x[1:]))
        needs = tracers[:1] if kind == "slice" else []
    missing = [n for n in needs if n not in known]
    if missing:
        raise PlanError(f"--needs names IDs that this plan does not have: {', '.join(missing)}. "
                        f"Next: `scripts/plan dag` lists the IDs")
    if not done:
        raise PlanError(f"{sid} needs at least one item. Next: add --done \"[auto] …\"")
    limit = MAX_ITEMS.get(prefix)
    if limit and len(done) > limit:
        split = "more tracers, or move the rest to slices" if prefix == "T" else "more slices"
        raise PlanError(f"{sid}: a {kind} has at most {limit} items ({len(done)} given), so that one "
                        f"session can finish it. Next: split it into {split}")
    items = [parse_item(d) for d in done]
    if demo and not (p.root / demo).is_file():
        raise PlanError(f"--demo {demo} is not a file of the repo. Next: give the path of the demo "
                        f"script, or leave --demo out")
    doc["nodes"].append({"id": sid, "kind": kind, "title": name, "needs": needs, "branch": None,
                         "status": "todo", "updated": dshm.today(), "next": nxt, "merge": None,
                         "why": why.strip(), "cuts": cuts.strip(), "not": not_.strip(),
                         "demo": demo or None, "log": []})
    p.slices[sid] = {"id": sid, "items": items}
    return sid


def cmd_add(p, a):
    need_main()
    if a.kind == "exit":
        it = parse_item(a.name if a.name.lstrip().startswith("[") else f"[human] {a.name}")
        if it["tier"] != "human":
            raise PlanError("exit items are [human] only. Next: add it to a slice instead")
        p.doc.setdefault("exit", []).append(it)
        return p.save(a, "Plan: exit item")
    needs = None if a.needs is None else ID_RE.findall(a.needs)
    sid = add_node(p, a.kind, a.name, needs, read_body(a.why), read_body(a.cuts),
                   a.demo or "", a.done or [], read_body(a.not_))
    print(f"plan: new {a.kind} {sid}")
    return p.save(a, f"Plan: add {sid} ({a.name.strip()})")


def cmd_row(p, a):
    need_main()
    set_state(p.node(a.id), a.status, a.next)
    return p.save(a, f"Plan: {a.id} {a.status}")


def cmd_log(p, a):
    need_main()
    e = entry(a.title, read_body(a.body))
    p.doc.setdefault("log", []).append(e)
    return p.save(a, f"Plan log: {e['title']}")


def add_pending(doc, sid, kind, item, branch="main", ref="—"):
    rows = doc.setdefault("pending", [])
    n = max((r["n"] for r in rows), default=0) + 1
    rows.append({"n": n, "slice": sid, "kind": kind, "item": item, "branch": branch, "ref": ref})
    return n


def cmd_pending(p, a):
    need_main()
    n = add_pending(p.doc, a.slice, a.kind, a.item, a.branch, a.commit_ref or "—")
    return p.save(a, f"Plan: pending {n} ({a.slice} {a.kind})")


def cmd_fix(p, a):
    """A bug that the user reported becomes a fix slice."""
    need_main()
    name, bug = a.name.strip().rstrip("."), " ".join(a.bug.split()).rstrip(".")
    sid = add_node(
        p, "slice", f"Fix: {name}", ID_RE.findall(a.needs or ""),
        why=f"The user reported a bug on {dshm.today()}: {bug}.",
        cuts="Find the cause. Fix it. Add a test that fails without the fix.",
        done=["[auto] A test reproduces the reported bug and passes with the fix",
              "[human] The user no longer sees the bug"],
        not_="Other changes. Report other bugs to the coordinator as new fix slices.",
        nxt=f"Fix: {name}; start a fix session")
    print(f"plan: new fix slice {sid}")
    return p.save(a, f"Plan: {sid} fix slice ({name})")


def cmd_assign(p, a):
    need_main()
    node = p.node(a.id)
    if a.round is not None:
        previous = node.get("round", 0)
        if not a.schedule or not previous < a.round <= 3:
            raise PlanError(f"cannot start {a.id} round {a.round} after {previous}. "
                            "Next: refresh scripts/run-plan-args and check the three-round limit")
        node["round"] = a.round
    if a.schedule:
        a.branch = node["branch"] or f"claude/{a.id.lower()}-{dshm.git('rev-parse', '--short', 'HEAD')}"
    if not a.branch or not re.search(rf"(^|/){a.id.lower()}(-|$)", a.branch):
        raise PlanError(f"the branch of {a.id} names it (claude/{a.id.lower()}-…), not {a.branch}. "
                        f"Next: give such a branch")
    import importlib.machinery
    import importlib.util
    loader = importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader("slice_env", str(p.root / "scripts/slice-env"))
    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_loader("slice_env", loader)
    se = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
    loader.exec_module(se)
    if a.dry_run:
        raise PlanError("assign has no --dry-run (it writes the registry). Next: scripts/slice-env --list")
    row, new = se.assign(a.id, a.branch, a.decisions, p.root)
    if a.schedule and not new and node["branch"] == a.branch and node.get("status") == "doing":
        if a.round is not None:
            p.save(a, f"Plan: {a.id} round {a.round}")
        return start_branch(a.branch)
    p.extra_files.append(dshm.REGISTRY)
    node["branch"] = a.branch
    set_state(node, "doing", "Slice owner builds")
    where = f", worktree `{a.worktree}`" if a.worktree else ""
    base = f" (from `{a.from_commit}`)" if a.from_commit else ""
    body = (f"Branch `{a.branch}`{where}{base}, simulator `{row['sim']}`, DSHM_HOME `{row['home']}`, "
            f"bridge {row['bridge']}, web {row['web']}; second host {row['bridge2']}/{row['web2']}. "
            f"`eval \"$(scripts/slice-env {a.id})\"` exports them.")
    if not new:
        body += " Same resources as before."
    if a.note:
        body += " " + a.note.strip()
    p.doc.setdefault("log", []).append(entry(f"{a.id} assigned", body))
    rc = p.save(a, f"Plan: assign {a.id}")
    return start_branch(a.branch) if a.schedule and rc == 0 else rc


def start_branch(branch):
    if not dshm.git("show-ref", "--verify", "--hash", f"refs/heads/{branch}", check=False):
        dshm.git("branch", branch, "HEAD")
    return 0


def review_line(sid, short):
    files = sorted(glob.glob(f"{os.environ.get('DSHM_REVIEW_DIR', '/tmp/dshm-review')}/{sid}-*.txt"),
                   key=os.path.getmtime)
    if not files:
        return None
    f = files[-1]
    text = Path(f).read_text()
    result = "PASS" if "RESULT: PASS" in text else "FAIL" if "RESULT: FAIL" in text else "?"
    flaky = " (flaky parts listed there)" if "flaky" in text else ", no flaky part"
    commit = Path(f).stem.split("-", 1)[1]
    return f"`scripts/review {sid}` at `{commit}`: `RESULT: {result}`{flaky} (`{f}`)."


PROVISIONAL = re.compile(r"\(?provisional, pending user confirmation\)?", re.I)
BOLD_LEAD = re.compile(r"\*\*(.+?)\*\*:?\s*(.*)")


def provisional(text):
    """The summaries of the provisional choices of an ARCHITECTURE.md text: the bold lead of each
    line that says 'provisional, pending user confirmation' (in the lead or after it), without
    that phrase; when the lead is only the phrase, the start of the text after it."""
    out = []
    for line in (text or "").splitlines():
        m = BOLD_LEAD.search(line)
        if not m or not PROVISIONAL.search(line):
            continue
        lead = PROVISIONAL.sub("", m.group(1)).strip().rstrip(".:(, ")
        out.append(lead or m.group(2).split(". ")[0].strip()[:80])
    return out


def cmd_merged(p, a):
    need_main()
    root = p.root
    full = dshm.git("rev-parse", "--verify", f"{a.merge_commit}^{{commit}}", cwd=root)
    short = full[:7]
    parents = dshm.git("rev-list", "--parents", "-n", "1", full, cwd=root).split()[1:]
    if len(parents) < 2:
        raise PlanError(f"{short} is not a merge commit. Next: give the merge commit of {a.id} "
                        f"(`git log --merges -3 --oneline`)")
    # The merge commit skipped pre-commit: check its plan/ against the first parent.
    errs = plandata.change_errors(root, plandata.head_files(root, parents[0]), plandata.head_files(root, full))
    if errs:
        raise PlanError("plan/ of the merge commit breaks the rules:\n" + "\n".join(errs)
                        + "\nNext: ask the user; a merge that breaks plan/ needs their review")
    node = p.node(a.id)
    if node.get("merge") == short and node.get("status") in ("done", "review"):
        print(f"plan: {a.id} merge {short} already recorded")
        if not a.keep:
            cleanup(root, a.id, full, cleanup_dry(a))
        return 0
    open_human = [it["text"] for it in p.items(a.id)["items"]
                  if it["tier"] == "human" and not any(e.startswith("human:") for e in it.get("evidence", []))]

    def arch(ref):
        r = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", str(root), "show", f"{ref}:ARCHITECTURE.md"], capture_output=True, text=True)
        return r.stdout if r.returncode == 0 else ""
    old = set(provisional(arch(parents[0])))
    added = [s for s in provisional(arch(full)) if s not in old]
    branch = node["branch"] or "—"
    rows = [add_pending(p.doc, a.id, "provisional", f"ARCHITECTURE.md: {s}", branch, f"merged {short}")
            for s in added]
    rows += [add_pending(p.doc, a.id, "[human]", desc, "main", short) for desc in open_human]
    if open_human:
        status = "review"
        nxt = f"User accepts {len(open_human)} [human] item{'s' if len(open_human) > 1 else ''} (pending)"
    else:
        status = "done"
        nxt = "— (provisional choices in pending)" if added else "—"
    set_state(node, status, nxt)
    node["merge"] = short
    parts = [f"Merged as `{short}`; the plan/ rules hold on the merge commit."]
    rl = review_line(a.id, short)
    if rl:
        parts.append(rl)
    parts.append(f"{len(open_human)} open [human] item(s), so {a.id} is `review`." if open_human
                 else f"No open [human] items, so {a.id} is `done`.")
    if rows:
        parts.append(f"Pending {', '.join(map(str, rows))}.")
    if a.note:
        parts.append(a.note.strip())
    p.doc.setdefault("log", []).append(entry(f"{a.id} merged", " ".join(parts)))
    rc = p.save(a, f"Plan: {a.id} {status}")
    if rc == 0 and not a.keep:
        cleanup(root, a.id, full, cleanup_dry(a))
    return rc


# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- cleanup
# After a merge, remove what the slice left on the Mac. Each destructive call
# goes through destroy(): with DSHM_CLEANUP_DRY=1 (or --dry-run) it prints and deletes nothing.

def cleanup_dry(a):
    return bool(getattr(a, "dry_run", False)) or os.environ.get("DSHM_CLEANUP_DRY") == "1"


def destroy(dry, what, *steps):
    """Run steps (argv lists, or ("rm", path)) to remove <what>. Returns True when removed."""
    if dry:
        print(f"plan: cleanup: would remove {what}")
        return True
    for step in steps:
        try:
            if step[0] == "rm":
                path = Path(step[1])
                if path.is_symlink() or path.is_file():
                    path.unlink()
                elif path.is_dir():
                    shutil.rmtree(path)
                continue
            check = step[0] != "-"          # "-" prefix: a failure does not matter (shutdown)
            argv = step[1:] if not check else step
            r = subprocess.run(argv, capture_output=True, text=True)
            if check and r.returncode != 0:
                print(f"plan: cleanup: left {what}: {' '.join(argv)} failed: {(r.stderr or r.stdout).strip()}")
                return False
        except OSError as e:
            print(f"plan: cleanup: left {what}: {e}")
            return False
    print(f"plan: cleanup: removed {what}")
    return True


def cleanup(root, sid, target, dry):
    """Remove the simulator, /tmp dirs, worktrees, branches and DSHM_HOME of slice <sid>.
    A worktree or branch goes only when its HEAD is an ancestor of <target> and it is clean."""
    reg = [r for r in dshm.parse_registry((root / dshm.REGISTRY).read_text()) if r["id"] == sid] \
        if (root / dshm.REGISTRY).exists() else []
    row = reg[-1] if reg else {}
    if reg and (root / plandata.PLAN_FILE).exists():
        branch = plandata.find_node(plandata.read_plan(root), sid).get("branch")
        if row["branch"] != branch:
            print(f"plan: cleanup: resources belong to {row['branch']}, not the current assignment; left them in place")
            return
    left = 0

    # 1. Simulator dshm-<ID> (each device with that name, by UDID).
    sim = row.get("sim") or f"dshm-{sid}"
    owner = Path(os.environ.get("DSHM_OWNERS", "/tmp/dshm-guard")) / sim   # the guard's record
    pid = owner.read_text().split()[0] if owner.is_file() and owner.read_text().split() else ""
    if pid.isdigit() and subprocess.run(["kill", "-0", pid], capture_output=True).returncode == 0:
        print(f"plan: cleanup: left simulator {sim}: a demo or review (pid {pid}) owns it")
        left += 1
    elif sim.startswith("dshm-"):
        for d in dshm.simulators():
            if d["name"] == sim:
                destroy(dry, f"simulator {sim} ({d['udid']})",
                        ["-", "xcrun", "simctl", "shutdown", d["udid"]],
                        ["xcrun", "simctl", "delete", d["udid"]])

    # 2. /tmp/dshm-<id> and /tmp/dshm-<id>-*. Not while a process uses them: the review of
    #    another slice can run the demo of this slice as a regression.
    key = sid.lower()
    ps = [l.strip() for l in subprocess.run(["ps", "-axo", "command="], capture_output=True, text=True).stdout.split("\n")
          if l.strip() and "scripts/plan" not in l]
    for path in dshm.slice_tmp_paths(sid):
        users = [l for l in ps if re.search(rf"{re.escape(path.name)}(?![\w.-])|scripts/demo/{key}\.sh", l)]
        if users:
            print(f"plan: cleanup: left {path}: a process uses it ({users[0][:80]})")
            left += 1
        else:
            destroy(dry, str(path), ("rm", str(path)))

    # 3. Worktrees and branches of the slice, only when merged into <target> and clean.
    here = {str(root), str(dshm.main_checkout())}
    wts = dshm.worktree_entries(cwd=root)
    reg_branch = row.get("branch")
    historical = {r["branch"] for r in reg[:-1] if r["branch"] != reg_branch}
    branches = [b for b in dshm.slice_branches(sid, cwd=root) if b not in historical]
    if reg_branch and reg_branch not in branches and \
            dshm.git("rev-parse", "--verify", "-q", f"refs/heads/{reg_branch}", cwd=root, check=False):
        branches.append(reg_branch)

    def merged(commit):
        return subprocess.run(["git", "merge-base", "--is-ancestor", commit, target], cwd=root).returncode == 0

    for br in branches:
        tip = dshm.git("rev-parse", br, cwd=root)
        holders = [w for w in wts if w["branch"] == br and w["path"] not in here]
        if any(w["branch"] == br and w["path"] in here for w in wts):
            print(f"plan: cleanup: left branch {br}: it is checked out here")
            left += 1
            continue
        if not merged(tip):
            where = f" and worktree {holders[0]['path']}" if holders else ""
            print(f"plan: cleanup: left branch {br}{where}: {tip[:7]} is not merged into {target[:7]}")
            left += 1
            continue
        ok = True
        for w in holders:
            dirty = subprocess.run(["git", "--no-optional-locks", "-C", w["path"], "status", "--porcelain"],
                                   capture_output=True, text=True)
            if dirty.returncode != 0:
                print(f"plan: cleanup: left worktree {w['path']}: git status failed")
                ok = False
            elif dirty.stdout.strip():
                n = len(dirty.stdout.strip().split("\n"))
                print(f"plan: cleanup: left worktree {w['path']} ({br}): {n} uncommitted or untracked file(s)")
                ok = False
            elif not destroy(dry, f"worktree {w['path']} ({br})", ["git", "-C", str(root), "worktree", "remove", w["path"]]):
                ok = False
        if not ok:
            left += 1
            continue
        if not destroy(dry, f"branch {br}", ["git", "-C", str(root), "branch", "-d", br]):
            left += 1

    # 4. DSHM_HOME, only inside ~/.dshm/.
    home = row.get("home")
    if home:
        safe = dshm.safe_slice_home(home)
        if safe is None:
            print(f"plan: cleanup: left DSHM_HOME {home}: it is not inside ~/.dshm/")
            left += 1
        elif os.path.lexists(safe):
            destroy(dry, f"DSHM_HOME {safe}", ("rm", safe))

    if left:
        print(f"plan: cleanup: {left} thing(s) left; remove them by hand when they are not needed")
    return 0



def cmd_cleanup(p, a):
    need_main()
    target = dshm.git("rev-parse", "--verify", "main^{commit}", cwd=p.root)
    if not p.exists:   # no plan: every slice of the last one is over; cleanup keeps its own checks
        return cleanup(p.root, a.id, target, cleanup_dry(a))
    status = p.node(a.id).get("status", "todo")
    if status not in ("review", "done"):
        raise PlanError(f"{a.id} is {status}; cleanup is only for a merged slice (review or done). "
                        f"Next: merge it first, then `scripts/plan merged {a.id} <merge-commit>`")
    return cleanup(p.root, a.id, target, cleanup_dry(a))


def cmd_evidence(p, a):
    need_slice_branch(a.id)
    p.node(a.id)
    it = item_at(p.items(a.id)["items"], a.n, a.id)
    if it["tier"] == "human":
        raise PlanError(f"item {a.n} of {a.id} is [human]: only the user accepts it. "
                        f"Next: leave it open; the coordinator lists it for the user")
    ptr = a.pointer.strip()
    ev = it.setdefault("evidence", [])
    if ptr in ev:
        print("plan: no change")
        return 0
    ev.append(ptr)
    return p.save(a, f"Plan {a.id}: evidence for item {a.n}")


def user_confirms(question, answer):
    """Refuse unless the user types `answer` on the controlling terminal."""
    try:
        tty_in, tty_out = open("/dev/tty"), open("/dev/tty", "w")
    except OSError:
        raise PlanError("only the user records a [human] item, from a terminal. "
                        "Next: the user runs this in their own terminal")
    with tty_in, tty_out:
        tty_out.write(f"{question}\nType {answer} to confirm: ")
        tty_out.flush()
        typed = tty_in.readline().strip()
    if typed != answer:
        raise PlanError(f"not confirmed (typed {typed!r}, not {answer!r}). "
                        f"Next: the user runs it again and types {answer}")


def cmd_accept(p, a):
    if a.id == "exit":
        items, where = p.doc.setdefault("exit", []), "exit"
    else:
        p.node(a.id)
        items, where = p.items(a.id)["items"], a.id
    it = item_at(items, a.n, where)
    if it["tier"] != "human":
        raise PlanError(f"item {a.n} of {where} is [{it['tier']}]: the verifier decides it. "
                        f"Next: add evidence with `scripts/plan evidence`")
    if not a.dry_run:
        user_confirms(f"Record item {a.n} of {where} as accepted by you: {it['text']}", where)
    it.setdefault("evidence", []).append(f"human:{dshm.today()} {' '.join(a.note.split())}")
    return p.save(a, f"Plan {where}: the user accepts item {a.n}", agent=False)


def cmd_slice_log(p, a):
    need_slice_branch(a.id)
    e = entry(a.title, read_body(a.body))
    p.node(a.id).setdefault("log", []).append(e)
    return p.save(a, f"Plan {a.id}: log, {e['title']}")


def cmd_slice_status(p, a):
    need_slice_branch(a.id)
    set_state(p.node(a.id), a.status)
    return p.save(a, f"Plan {a.id}: status {a.status}")


def main():
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="scripts/plan", description="Bookkeeping in plan/ (see the file header).")
    common = argparse.ArgumentParser(add_help=False)
    common.add_argument("--commit", action="store_true", help="commit the change")
    common.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true", help="print the diff, change nothing")
    sub = ap.add_subparsers(dest="cmd", required=True)

    def add(name, fn):
        sp = sub.add_parser(name, parents=[common])
        sp.set_defaults(fn=fn)
        return sp

    sp = add("show", cmd_show); sp.add_argument("id")
    sp = add("title", cmd_title); sp.add_argument("--milestone")
    add("lint", cmd_lint)
    sp = add("dag", cmd_dag); sp.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    sp = add("passed", cmd_passed); sp.add_argument("id"); sp.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    sp.add_argument("--base", default="HEAD")
    sp = add("verify", cmd_verify); sp.add_argument("id"); sp.add_argument("--base", default="HEAD")
    sp = add("merge", cmd_merge); sp.add_argument("id"); sp.add_argument("--into", required=True)
    sp.add_argument("--allow-changed-evidence", dest="allow", action="append", default=[], metavar="PATH")
    sp = add("new", cmd_new); sp.add_argument("title")
    sp = add("add", cmd_add); sp.add_argument("kind", choices=[*KINDS, "exit"]); sp.add_argument("name")
    sp.add_argument("--why", default=""); sp.add_argument("--cuts", default="")
    sp.add_argument("--demo", default=""); sp.add_argument("--not", dest="not_", default="")
    sp.add_argument("--done", action="append"); sp.add_argument("--needs")
    sp = add("row", cmd_row); sp.add_argument("id"); sp.add_argument("status"); sp.add_argument("--next")
    sp = add("log", cmd_log); sp.add_argument("title"); sp.add_argument("--body")
    sp = add("fix", cmd_fix); sp.add_argument("name"); sp.add_argument("--bug", required=True)
    sp.add_argument("--needs")
    sp = add("pending", cmd_pending); sp.add_argument("slice"); sp.add_argument("kind"); sp.add_argument("item")
    sp.add_argument("--branch", default="main"); sp.add_argument("--commit-ref")
    sp = add("assign", cmd_assign); sp.add_argument("id"); sp.add_argument("--branch")
    sp.add_argument("--round", type=int, help="reserve this build round before it starts")
    sp.add_argument("--schedule", action="store_true", help="assign and create the scheduler branch")
    sp.add_argument("--worktree"); sp.add_argument("--from", dest="from_commit")
    sp.add_argument("--decisions", type=int, default=dshm.DECISION_BLOCK, help=argparse.SUPPRESS)
    sp.add_argument("--note")
    sp = add("merged", cmd_merged); sp.add_argument("id"); sp.add_argument("merge_commit", metavar="merge-commit")
    sp.add_argument("--note"); sp.add_argument("--keep", action="store_true", help="skip the cleanup")
    sp = add("cleanup", cmd_cleanup); sp.add_argument("id")
    sp = add("evidence", cmd_evidence); sp.add_argument("id"); sp.add_argument("n", type=int)
    sp.add_argument("pointer")
    sp = add("accept", cmd_accept); sp.add_argument("id"); sp.add_argument("n", type=int); sp.add_argument("note")
    sp = add("slice-log", cmd_slice_log); sp.add_argument("id"); sp.add_argument("title"); sp.add_argument("--body")
    sp = add("slice-status", cmd_slice_status); sp.add_argument("id"); sp.add_argument("status")

    a = ap.parse_args()
    try:
        if getattr(a, "id", None) and not (a.fn is cmd_accept and a.id == "exit"):
            dshm.check_id(a.id)
        p = Plan(dshm.toplevel())
        if a.fn not in (cmd_new, cmd_cleanup, cmd_dag, cmd_passed, cmd_verify, cmd_merge, cmd_lint):
            p.load()
        return a.fn(p, a)
    except PlanError as e:
        print(f"plan: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
